  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 95e66c6366d904e98bc83428217d4fd7, type: 3}
  m_Name: Voyage - the helm is yours
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.VisualScripting.Flow::Unity.VisualScripting.ScriptGraphAsset
  _data:
    _json: '{"graph":{"variables":{"Kind":"Flow","collection":{"$content":[],"$version":"A"},"$version":"A"},"controlInputDefinitions":[],"controlOutputDefinitions":[],"valueInputDefinitions":[],"valueOutputDefinitions":[],"title":"Voyage - the helm is yours","summary":"In the 3D view your hand takes the helm (A and D, or the mouse held to a side), she answers it, and her charted course waits (Code/Game/Voyage/HandHelm.cs; the turning is ChartBody.Move''s, the keys ShipStageHook''s). When the helm is given back (H, or the swap to the chart) the steersman lays her course again from where she is, or she lies to; the log is told. How fast she answers, and whether he lays her course again, are the rule graphs'' (Game/Graphs/Rules).","pan":{"x":0.0,"y":0.0},"zoom":1.0,"elements":[{"coroutine":false,"defaultValues":{},"position":{"x":0.0,"y":0.0},"guid":"7f0fa41a-2240-477f-85b9-079bb13fe47e","$version":"A","$type":"Kapman.Graphs.OnTheHelm","$id":"9"},{"defaultValues":{},"position":{"x":460.0,"y":0.0},"guid":"de6dcfec-48be-4146-ad37-a7ee029eabf2","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.If","$id":"11"},{"defaultValues":{},"position":{"x":860.0,"y":-40.0},"guid":"e8404510-1575-4790-a46d-c471abe25b3f","$version":"A","$type":"Kapman.Graphs.HelmLayAgain","$id":"13"},{"defaultValues":{"words":{"$content":"","$type":"System.String"}},"position":{"x":1360.0,"y":-40.0},"guid":"a5190a80-d86a-48a8-9af1-70f68ed226f3","$version":"A","$type":"Kapman.Graphs.HelmSay","$id":"15"},{"defaultValues":{"words":{"$content":"","$type":"System.String"}},"position":{"x":1360.0,"y":100.0},"guid":"18542d58-dcb9-4276-83ab-99b14e028061","$version":"A","$type":"Kapman.Graphs.HelmSay","$id":"17"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"9"},"sourceKey":"trigger","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"11"},"destinationKey":"enter","guid":"9b0379ed-2a29-4950-8d3e-6d631d0699f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ControlConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"11"},"sourceKey":"ifTrue","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"13"},"destinationKey":"enter","guid":"d5f62e96-3058-4b83-b0a9-fbb0fefbaba3","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ControlConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"13"},"sourceKey":"exit","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"15"},"destinationKey":"enter","guid":"62505df0-36c9-4c66-9186-cc5489bc991b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ControlConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"11"},"sourceKey":"ifFalse","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"17"},"destinationKey":"enter","guid":"df6c14c5-522f-4747-b143-70ec29d21c4a","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ControlConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"9"},"sourceKey":"givenBack","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"11"},"destinationKey":"condition","guid":"80947d54-77fb-436a-8c2b-b3643cc35240","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"13"},"sourceKey":"words","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"15"},"destinationKey":"words","guid":"7cb9b470-0ccb-4282-9f47-098a256c9d40","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"sourceUnit":{"$ref":"9"},"sourceKey":"words","destinationUnit":{"$ref":"17"},"destinationKey":"words","guid":"5d4e71dd-3d28-464e-b59e-b02ab7eb68cc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.ValueConnection"},{"position":{"xMin":-40.0,"yMin":-90.0,"xMax":2260.0,"yMax":330.0},"label":"The helm is yours","comment":"Your ruling of 13 October 2026: steer her yourself in the 3D view. (It overturns the rulings of 26 September and 10 October that her bow is not turned by hand.)","color":{"r":0.32,"g":0.55,"b":0.32,"a":1.0},"guid":"625d01fa-2bfa-4a8f-bb41-4bc73dcbe05a","$version":"A","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.GraphGroup"},{"position":{"xMin":-20.0,"yMin":200.0,"xMax":540.0,"yMax":460.0},"title":"The moments","body":"taken: your hand is on the helm; her charted course waits.\nlet_go: the helm is amidships again; she holds her heading (nothing is said).\ngiven_back: the helm is the steersman''s again (H, or the swap back to the chart): he lays her course again from where she is, or she lies to.\naground: your hand has run her aground; the helm is let go, and the getting off is as it always was (the Aground graph).","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"97c6b5c7-d64a-4c4d-971e-b2fd339dc24d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":580.0,"yMin":200.0,"xMax":1140.0,"yMax":460.0},"title":"The words","body":"The words come with the event, or from the laying (\"The helm is the steersman''s again: her course is laid again from where she is, 98 km, about 1.2 days.\"): PLACEHOLDER WORDS, in HandHelm.cs, the user''s to write. The clock does not drop back for the helm: it is the player''s own hand.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"9d5da98f-c08b-488a-96f9-30819e8d8cfa","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":1180.0,"yMin":200.0,"xMax":1740.0,"yMax":460.0},"title":"What is not here","body":"The keys and the mouse (ShipStageHook), how she turns and makes way under your hand (ChartBody.Move), and the laying by the lanes (Adrift.LayAgain, Course.SetTo) are the code''s. How fast she answers the helm, and whether the steersman lays her course again when it is given back, are the rule graphs.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"00a1c79c-49f7-45e7-bfcd-410b279dac9f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"}],"$version":"A"}}'
    _objectReferences: []
